      "text": "15min.lt investigators filmed 13 EU-funded farmer training sessions over five months — all held in empty or near-empty rooms. The sessions were organized by Mokslinės Paslaugos, an institution owned solely by Vigilijus Jukna (PM Ruginienė's public affairs adviser and current LSDP member). Jukna also serves as chancellor of VDU Agricultural Academy, which received a separate €285k from similar EU programs. Potential document falsification was identified: names of absent participants appeared in attendance records at one VDU-run session. The National Paying Agency had conducted only remote inspections and found no serious violations. Ruginienė dismissed Jukna the same day the story broke; she told media the matter 'must be investigated by law enforcement.' FNTT and STT subsequently opened pre-trial investigations and searched premises. President Nausėda called on the PM to address the matter. Former Parliament speaker Arūnas Valinskas publicly praised Ruginienée for 'acting before the evening news.'",
